Markus "'''pronax'''" Wallstén  {{born}} is a [[retired]] [[:Category:Sweden|Swedish]] professional ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' and ''[[Counter-Strike]]'' player. He is best known for leading [[Fnatic]] from November 2013 to November 2015, during which the team was widely regarded as the best in the world, winning three [[Majors|Major]] championships and nine other S-Tier tournaments. In April 2016, pronax founded the esports organization [[GODSENT]].

==Achievements==
{{Player achievements table|player=pronax}}

==Trivia==
*In-game leader-wise, despite previously playing in teams like [[H2k Gaming]] and [[ESC Gaming]] with other dedicated in-game leaders such as Richard "[[Xizt]]" Landström and Finn "[[karrigan]]" Andersen in the past, he has assumed control of this role each time. He was also the in-game leader of [[Team Sweden]] over [[Xizt]] during their tournament run at [[The World Championships 2015]]. The only team where he wasn't the in-game leader was in [[n!faculty]], where Lukas "[[gla1ve]]" Rossander took the role.

